---

<BaseLayout
  title="Style guide — Social Magent"
  description="Internal design system reference for Social Magent. Not indexed."
  path="/styleguide"
  noindex={true}
>
  <!-- ============================ INTRO ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <Overline text="Social Magent — design system" />
      <h1 class="sg-section__title" style="font-size: var(--fs-h2); margin-top: var(--space-2);">
        Style guide
      </h1>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        The complete design language: tokens, typography, components and patterns.
        Everything on this page is built from <code>src/styles/tokens.css</code> — change
        colours, fonts and spacing there and the whole site follows.
      </p>
      <Notice variant="info" title="Placeholder content">
        Every name, date, headline and image on this page is a clearly-labelled placeholder.
        Nothing here is a real claim, client, person or statistic.
      </Notice>

      <p class="sg-sub">Typeface choice</p>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        <strong>IBM Plex Sans</strong> (UI) and <strong>Source Serif 4</strong> (editorial
        headlines) — both free, open-licence (SIL OFL) families, self-hosted through
        Fontsource so the site makes no external font requests. Plex Sans is a precise,
        engineered sans that reads as corporate without being generic; Source Serif 4 is a
        high-contrast reading serif that gives headlines an editorial, advisory-firm
        authority. Serif is reserved for headlines and pull quotes; all UI and body copy
        stays in the sans.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ COLOUR ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="sg-section__title">Colour</h2>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        One near-black ink, a neutral grey scale, white and an off-white surface, one
        signature accent (indigo-violet — used sparingly), and accessible feedback
        colours. Ratios are measured against WCAG AA (4.5:1 body text, 3:1 large text).
      </p>

      <p class="sg-sub">Neutrals</p>
      <div class="sg-grid">
        {
          neutrals.map((c) => (
            <div class="swatch">
              <div class="swatch__chip" style={`background:${c.hex};`} />
              <div class="swatch__meta">
                <div class="swatch__name">{c.name}</div>
                <div class="swatch__hex">{c.hex}</div>
                <div class="swatch__ratio">{c.ratio}</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Signature accent</p>
      <div class="sg-grid">
        {
          accents.map((c) => (
            <div class="swatch">
              <div class="swatch__chip" style={`background:${c.hex};`} />
              <div class="swatch__meta">
                <div class="swatch__name">{c.name}</div>
                <div class="swatch__hex">{c.hex}</div>
                <div class="swatch__ratio">{c.ratio}</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Feedback colours</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        {
          semantics.map((c) => (
            <div class="swatch" style="min-width: 260px;">
              <div class="swatch__chip" style={`background:${c.bg}; border-bottom: 4px solid ${c.hex};`} />
              <div class="swatch__meta">
                <div class="swatch__name">{c.name}</div>
                <div class="swatch__hex">{c.hex} on {c.bg}</div>
                <div class="swatch__ratio">{c.ratio}</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Semantic aliases in the dark surface context</p>
      <div class="sg-dark">
        <p style="color: var(--color-text); max-width: none;">
          On <code>data-surface="dark"</code> the aliases re-point: text becomes grey-100
          (14.96:1), muted text grey-300, links accent-300 (7.32:1), borders grey-700.
          Components need no changes — they read the aliases.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ TYPOGRAPHY ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="sg-section__title">Typography</h2>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        Fluid scale with <code>clamp()</code> — mobile value → desktop value. Body 16px at
        1.6 line-height, headings tighter, body measure capped at ~70 characters.
      </p>
      {
        typeSpecimens.map((t) => (
          <div class="type-specimen">
            <div class="type-specimen__label">{t.label}</div>
            <div class={t.cls}>{t.text}</div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <p class="sg-sub">Fonts in use</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="flex: 1; min-width: 240px;">
          <p class="type-specimen__label">IBM Plex Sans Variable — UI, body, labels</p>
          <p style="font-size: var(--fs-h3); font-family: var(--font-sans); letter-spacing: normal;">
            ABCDEFGHIJKLM abcdefghijklm 0123456789
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="flex: 1; min-width: 240px;">
          <p class="type-specimen__label">Source Serif 4 Variable — headlines, quotes</p>
          <p style="font-size: var(--fs-h3); font-family: var(--font-serif);">
            ABCDEFGHIJKLM abcdefghijklm 0123456789
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ SPACING & LAYOUT ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="sg-section__title">Spacing, layout &amp; shape</h2>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        8px base rhythm. Section padding is fluid. Containers: content 720px, standard
        1200px, wide 1440px. Grid: 12 columns, 24px gutters. Radii 0–4px, hairline
        borders, almost no shadow.
      </p>

      <p class="sg-sub">Spacing scale (8px base)</p>
      <div class="spacing-scale">
        {
          spacing.map((s) => (
            <div class="spacing-scale__item">
              <span>
                <code>{s.token}</code> · {s.value}
              </span>
              <span class="spacing-scale__bar" style={`width:${s.px}px;`} />
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Section padding</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <div class="sg-demo"><code>--section-y-sm</code> compact band</div>
        <div class="sg-demo"><code>--section-y</code> standard section</div>
        <div class="sg-demo"><code>--section-y-lg</code> hero / statement</div>
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Containers</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--color-accent);">
          <code>--container-content</code> 720px
        </div>
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--color-accent);">
          <code>--container-standard</code> 1200px
        </div>
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--color-accent);">
          <code>--container-wide</code> 1440px
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">12-column grid (24px gutters)</p>
      <div class="sg-grid-demo">
        {Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => <span>{i + 1}</span>)}
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Borders, radii, shadows, motion</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="border: var(--border);">1px hairline border</div>
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="border: var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);">radius-sm 2px</div>
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="border: var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-md);">radius-md 4px</div>
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain" style="box-shadow: var(--shadow-1); border: var(--border);">shadow-1 (menus only use shadow-2)</div>
        <div class="sg-demo sg-demo--plain">150 / 200 / 250ms · cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ BUTTONS ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="sg-section__title">Buttons</h2>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        Primary (one per screen), secondary outline, text link with arrow. Hover and
        focus-visible states are live below; disabled and loading are shown explicitly.
      </p>

      <p class="sg-sub">Variants</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <Button variant="primary">Primary action</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary">Secondary action</Button>
        <Button variant="text">Text link with arrow</Button>
        <Button variant="primary" small>Small primary</Button>
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">States — hover / focus-visible (tab to see focus)</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <Button variant="primary">Hover me</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary">Hover me</Button>
        <Button variant="text">Hover me</Button>
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">States — disabled &amp; loading</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <Button variant="primary" disabled>Disabled</Button>
        <Button variant="secondary" disabled>Disabled</Button>
        <Button variant="primary" loading>Loading</Button>
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Buttons on the dark surface</p>
      <div class="sg-dark">
        <div class="sg-row">
          <Button variant="primary">Primary</Button>
          <Button variant="secondary">Secondary</Button>
          <Button variant="text">Text link →</Button>
          <Button variant="primary" disabled>Disabled</Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ HERO VARIANTS ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="sg-section__title">Hero variants</h2>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        (a) block hero with placeholder image, (b) light editorial hero, (c) compact page
        hero with breadcrumb. Shown here stacked; on real pages one hero per screen.
      </p>

      <p class="sg-sub">a) Block hero</p>
    </div>
    <Hero
      variant="block"
      overline="Placeholder overline"
      title="A large confident headline for a dark block hero."
      lead="Placeholder lead text introducing the section in one or two sentences."
    />

    <div class="container">
      <p class="sg-sub">b) Editorial hero (light)</p>
    </div>
    <Hero
      variant="editorial"
      overline="Placeholder overline"
      title="An editorial headline with two clear actions."
      lead="Placeholder lead paragraph. One primary action per screen keeps the choice obvious."
    />

    <div class="container">
      <p class="sg-sub">c) Compact page hero with breadcrumb</p>
    </div>
    <Hero
      variant="compact"
      title="Compact page title"
      lead="Placeholder page introduction."
      breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Insights' }]}
    />
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ CARDS ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="sg-section__title">Cards</h2>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        Flat surfaces with thin borders and small radii — no shadows. Insight card,
        feature card, capability card and horizontal list row.
      </p>

      <p class="sg-sub">Insight / article card</p>
      <div class="sg-grid" style="max-width: 760px;">
        <InsightCard
          category="Placeholder category"
          title="Placeholder insight headline for the card component"
          date="Placeholder date"
        />
        <InsightCard
          category="Placeholder category"
          title="A second placeholder headline to show wrapping"
          date="Placeholder date"
        />
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Feature card &amp; capability card</p>
      <div class="sg-grid">
        <FeatureCard index="01" title="Placeholder feature title">
          Placeholder description text for a feature card used in editorial grids.
        </FeatureCard>
        <CapabilityCard title="Placeholder capability">
          A stat-free capability description. No numbers, no claims — just a short
          explanation of what the capability covers.
        </CapabilityCard>
        <CapabilityCard title="Placeholder capability">
          Another capability placeholder, kept deliberately plain and flat.
        </CapabilityCard>
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Horizontal list rows</p>
      <div style="max-width: var(--container-content);">
        <ListRow title="Placeholder related item headline" meta="Placeholder date · Placeholder category" />
        <ListRow title="Another placeholder related item headline" meta="Placeholder date · Placeholder category" />
        <ListRow title="Third placeholder related item headline" meta="Placeholder date · Placeholder category" />
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Cards on the dark surface</p>
      <div class="sg-dark">
        <div class="sg-grid">
          <CapabilityCard title="Placeholder capability">
            Capability card on a dark band — it reads the semantic aliases.
          </CapabilityCard>
          <CapabilityCard title="Placeholder capability">
            Borders and text adapt automatically.
          </CapabilityCard>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ SECTION PATTERNS ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="sg-section__title">Section patterns</h2>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        Split section, three-column capabilities, featured insight with related list,
        quiet CTA bands (light and dark) and the leadership grid.
      </p>

      <p class="sg-sub">Split section (text + media)</p>
      <SplitSection
        overline="Placeholder overline"
        title="Split section headline"
        buttonLabel="Secondary action"
      >
        Placeholder body copy for the split pattern. The media side is a clearly-labelled
        abstract placeholder — no stock photography.
      </SplitSection>

      <p class="sg-sub">Three-column capabilities</p>
      <Capabilities
        overline="Placeholder overline"
        title="Three-column capabilities"
        intro="Placeholder introduction sentence for the capabilities pattern."
      >
        <CapabilityCard title="Placeholder capability one">
          Placeholder description of the first capability.
        </CapabilityCard>
        <CapabilityCard title="Placeholder capability two">
          Placeholder description of the second capability.
        </CapabilityCard>
        <CapabilityCard title="Placeholder capability three">
          Placeholder description of the third capability.
        </CapabilityCard>
      </Capabilities>

      <p class="sg-sub">Featured insight + related list</p>
      <FeaturedInsight
        title="Placeholder featured insight headline"
        date="Placeholder date · Placeholder category"
        related={[
          { title: 'Placeholder related item', meta: 'Placeholder date' },
          { title: 'Placeholder related item', meta: 'Placeholder date' },
          { title: 'Placeholder related item', meta: 'Placeholder date' },
        ]}
      >
        Placeholder standfirst for the featured insight pattern.
      </FeaturedInsight>

      <p class="sg-sub">Leadership grid (placeholder portraits)</p>
      <LeadershipGrid />
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
      <p class="container sg-sub" style="margin-top: 0;">Quiet CTA band — light</p>
      <CtaBand title="Placeholder call to action headline" buttonLabel="Talk to us">
        Placeholder supporting line. One action per band.
      </CtaBand>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
      <p class="container sg-sub" style="margin-top: 0;">Quiet CTA band — dark variant</p>
      <CtaBand
        title="Placeholder call to action headline"
        buttonLabel="Talk to us"
        variant="dark"
      >
        Placeholder supporting line on the dark surface.
      </CtaBand>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ FORMS ============================ -->
  <section class="sg-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="sg-section__title">Forms</h2>
      <p class="sg-section__intro">
        Visible labels, helper text, error and success states, 44px targets, keyboard
        friendly with a visible focus ring. Placeholders are examples only — never a
        replacement for a label.
      </p>

      <div class="sg-grid" style="align-items: start;">
        <Input
          label="Text input"
          name="demo-text"
          placeholder="Placeholder input"
          helper="Helper text explains the expected format."
        />
        <Input
          label="Email address"
          name="demo-email-error"
          type="email"
          state="error"
          message="Enter a valid email address."
          required
        />
        <Input
          label="Email address"
          name="demo-email-success"
          type="email"
          state="success"
          message="Looks good."
        />
        <Select
          label="Select"
          name="demo-select"
          helper="Choose one option."
          options={[
            { label: 'Placeholder option one', value: '1' },
            { label: 'Placeholder option two', value: '2' },
            { label: 'Placeholder option three', value: '3' },
          ]}
        />
        <Textarea
          label="Textarea"
          name="demo-textarea"
          placeholder="Placeholder message"
          helper="Tell us what you need."
        />
        <FileUpload label="File upload" name="demo-file" hint="Placeholder: PDF or DOCX, up to 10 MB." />
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Checkbox &amp; radio</p>
      <div class="sg-row" style="gap: var(--space-6);">
        <fieldset class="choice-group">
          <legend class="choice-group__legend">Checkbox group</legend>
          <Checkbox label="Placeholder choice one" name="demo-check-1" />
          <Checkbox label="Placeholder choice two" name="demo-check-2" checked helper="With helper text." />
          <Checkbox label="Disabled choice" name="demo-check-3" />
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset class="choice-group">
          <legend class="choice-group__legend">Radio group</legend>
          <Radio label="Placeholder option A" name="demo-radio" value="a" checked />
          <Radio label="Placeholder option B" name="demo-radio" value="b" />
          <Radio label="Placeholder option C" name="demo-radio" value="c" />
        </fieldset>
      </div>

      <p class="sg-sub">Forms on the dark surface</p>
      <div class="sg-dark">
        <div class="sg-grid" style="align-items: start;">
          <Input label="Text input" name="demo-dark-text" placeholder="Placeholder input" helper="Helper text on dark." />
          <Input label="Email address" name="demo-dark-email" type="email" state="error" message="Enter a valid email address." />
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: var(--space-3);">
          <Checkbox label="Placeholder checkbox on dark" name="demo-dark-check" checked />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
